# health v2.8 — WARNING. "entered-in-error" written to the CLINICAL status of an
# allergy. This is the load-bearing case of the whole status family.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT VALUE. "entered-in-error" is a real code, and it is in three of
# the five value sets v1.16 binds: it is legal on a lab result, on a vital sign
# and on a document. It is NOT in AllergyIntolerance.clinicalStatus, which has
# exactly three codes, and its exclusion is the one deliberate narrowing in the
# release. The reason is stated at the constraint: admitting it beside "inactive"
# and "resolved" would merge "the patient no longer reacts to this" with "this
# allergy was never real", which are opposite clinical facts and the one pair a
# safety-relevant record must never conflate.
#
# So this fixture is not testing that a shape rejects nonsense. Every other WARN
# fixture in this batch uses a value that is wrong everywhere. This one uses a
# value that is right in three other places and wrong here, which is the only
# way to show that the allergy set is three codes BY CHOICE rather than by
# oversight -- and it is what fails if someone later "completes" the set to
# four to match its siblings.
#
# The repudiation this record is reaching for has a correct home, and the
# fixture shows it: clinical:verificationStatus, a different element with a
# different four-code value set that does contain "entered-in-error".
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet. Nothing rejects this
# record, and the fixture asserts exactly that alongside the warning.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:a11e0208-0000-4000-8000-000000000002> a health:AllergyRecord ;
    health:allergen "Amoxicillin" ;
    health:reaction "Urticaria" ;
    clinical:status "entered-in-error" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
